# Anticipate workflow blockers (do not wait for Jerry's error)

Jerry is not QA. If you can see where he is working and what he will click next, **clear the path before he gets an error**.

## Hard lesson (2026-07-25)

Jerry was on **Review & Approve → American Express → January 2026**. Integrity already showed January **closed**. The agent kept editing categories/rules and waited until Jerry hit:

> Cannot post to closed period …

That wasted his time. **Wrong.**

## Required anticipation

When Jerry (or the conversation) is in **Review & Approve / draft-journals / CAT-APPR**:

1. Immediately check which months in the queue are `CLOSED` via period integrity.
2. If any waiting charges fall in closed months, **fix posting before he tries**:
   - Prefer product path: CAT-APPR post may briefly reopen → post → re-close (`lib/post-journal.js`).
   - Verify with a live post (or dry integrity + code path) — do not assume.
3. Do not stop at “period is closed” as an explanation while he is actively approving that month — **make approve/post work**.

## General pattern

Before finishing any accounting UI/workflow change:

- Ask: “What will Jerry click next?”
- Ask: “What will fail if I do nothing?”
- Clear that failure now (code, reopen/reclose, seed rule, deploy, verify).

Never require Jerry to screenshot an error you could have predicted from API state + the screen he is on.
